<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mangkunegara VII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mangkunegara VII was prince of the Mangkunegaran principality in Surakarta from 1916 to 1944. Educated partly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, he supported Javanese cultural nationalism and was a celebrated patron of dance, gamelan music and wayang. In 1933 he founded one of the first indigenous radio stations in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, which broadcast Javanese music.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mangkunegara-vii.jpg" alt="Mangkunegara VII" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_vorst_Pangeran_Adipati_Ario_Mangkoe_Negoro_VII_TMnr_10001303.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
